# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We as members, contributors, and maintainers of this project pledge to make participation in our community a welcoming and respectful experience for everyone, regardless of background, identity, experience, or status.

We are committed to creating an open and friendly environment where everyone can contribute and communicate respectfully.

## Our Standards

Examples of behavior that contribute to a positive environment include:

* Using welcoming and inclusive language.
* Being respectful of different opinions and experiences.
* Accepting constructive criticism.
* Focusing on what is best for the community.
* Showing empathy and kindness toward other community members.

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, discrimination, personal attacks, inappropriate comments, or any other conduct that creates an unsafe or disrespectful environment.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of acceptable behavior. They may take appropriate and fair corrective action in response to behavior that violates this Code of Conduct.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies within project spaces and whenever an individual is officially representing the project or its community.

## Enforcement

Instances of abusive, harassing, or otherwise unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers. All reports will be reviewed and investigated fairly and appropriately.

Project maintainers have the right to remove, edit, or reject comments, commits, code, or other contributions that violate this Code of Conduct.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Project maintainers will consider the nature and seriousness of the violation when deciding on appropriate action. Possible responses may include:

1. A warning.
2. Removal of inappropriate content.
3. Temporary restriction from participating in the project.
4. Permanent removal from the project community.

Actions will be taken fairly and consistently.

